<title>USA: Marten sees profits through year-end.</title>
<headline>Marten sees profits through year-end.</headline>
<dateline>MONDOVI, Wis. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marten Transport Ltd said it is being hurt by fuel costs and increased competition, but expects to remain profitable through the year.</p>
<p>Randolph Marten, president of the trucking concern, said, &quot;Fuel costs and increased competition continue to affect our profits.&quot;</p>
<p>But he added, &quot;We're confident that our superior service and expense control procedures will yield profits for the remainder of the year.&quot;</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
